# Design System

All UI must follow this visual identity. Do not introduce competing palettes, decorative fonts, or theatrical motion.

Landing (`/` and `/intro`) stays on electric blue. Inner routes (`/home`, `/about`, `/work`, `/blog`, `/book`) use the inverted house pair until the user presses Spray.

## Palette

| Token | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Landing background | `#4545FF` | Gateway and RSVP canvas only |
| Landing text | `#DDDDFF` | Gateway and RSVP copy |
| Logo (gateway) | `#0B0CB4` | Idle lockup on the landing only |
| Inner background | `#DDDDFF` | Unsprayed factory pages |
| Inner text | `#4545FF` | Unsprayed factory copy and chrome |
| Logo (inner, unsprayed) | `#0B0CB4` | Nav lockup until Spray (`--brand-logo`) |
| Line numbers | `#D97706` | Factory gutter (`--syn-number`) |

Do not paint inner routes with landing electric blue as the unsprayed default. Spray is the only switch off the inverted pair.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — unsprayed inner canvas
<div className="bg-[#4545FF] text-[#DDDDFF]">

// ✅ GOOD — landing
<div className="bg-[#4545FF] text-[#DDDDFF]">

// ✅ GOOD — unsprayed inner
<div className="bg-[#DDDDFF] text-[#4545FF]">
```

## Grid

Use a 1px high-contrast structural grid. Borders and dividers on inner pages:

```
color-mix(in srgb, #4545FF 15%, transparent)
```

Treat layout as an engineering drawing: visible edges, aligned columns, no soft drop shadows or glassmorphism.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="border border-[color-mix(in_srgb,#4545FF_15%,transparent)]">
```

## Typography

- **Display / body:** sans-serif.
- **Metadata, labels, code snippets, UI controls** (buttons, inputs, nav, badges, timestamps): `font-mono` only.

Never set body copy in mono. Never set labels or controls in a rounded/display face.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="font-sans">Submit</button>
<p className="font-mono">We build software factories.</p>

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="font-mono">Submit</button>
<p className="font-sans">We build software factories.</p>
<span className="font-mono text-sm">RepDaily · in production</span>
```

## Motion

Reveals are clean and humble. Default Framer Motion pattern:

- `opacity: 0 → 1`
- `translateY(10px) → 0`

No bounce, spring-overshoot, large travel, or staggered spectacle unless a specific interaction requires it. Keep duration short (~0.4s) and easing understated.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<motion.div
  initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 10 }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
  transition={{ duration: 0.4, ease: "easeOut" }}
>
```
